an><span style=\"color:#066\">0.364</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>$Benefit<br>       a1    d1    d2    d3      c<br>par </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.498</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">4.529</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2.201</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1.23</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">-</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.894</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>$GroupPars<br>    MEAN_1 COV_11<br>par      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000\">      </span><span style=\"color:#066\">1</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div>How can I relate here these two sets of  parameters?<br> </div><div>Even the coef(mod_grsm, IRTpars=T) is returning the same output as above.<br></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
